 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 241179,
   "is_answer_order_important": true,
   "stimulus_html": "<figure class=\"unnumbered\">\n<img src=\"exercises/media/23015ba1c2343c2e.jpg\" alt=\"\">\n<figcaption>(credit: modification of work by Rafael Sanjuán, et al./<i>Journal of Virology</i>)</figcaption>\n</figure>",
   "stem_html": "<p>The graph shows the mutation rates of different viruses and bacteria. The ss stands for single strand, ds for double strand, and retro for retroviruses (RNA viruses which transcribe DNA and add it to host's DNA).</p>\n<p>Note the viroids at the top left of the graph. These particles infect flowering plants. Based on the trends in this graph, make a prediction about viroid structure.</p>",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 754180,
     "content_html": "Viroids have comparatively large sizes and complex genomes."
    },
    {
     "id": 754179,
     "content_html": "Viroids have large sizes, but have tiny genomes."
    },
    {
     "id": 754178,
     "content_html": "Viroids have a large genome packed in a small structure."
    },
    {
     "id": 754181,
     "content_html": "Viroids have small genomes and are extremely small."
    }
   ],
